.TH CTI-KEV 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-kev \- CISA KEV remediation deadlines for vulnerabilities the scanner found here
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti-kev
.RB [ \-\-enriched
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-horizon
.IR DAYS ]
.RB [ \-\-hosts ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-quiet ]
.RB [ \-\-fail\-if\-overdue ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-kev
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-kev
reads one enriched findings file written by the daily digest's enrich step
and reports the CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities deadlines (BOD 22\-01
due dates) that apply to this estate.
It is run by hand, by the orchestrator during a heartbeat, or from
.BR "task kev" ;
no timer runs it. The daily digest carries the same deadlines itself.
.PP
Only findings the scanner actually detected count: status
.B PRESENT
with at least one host. Each such finding with a
.B kev_due
date is placed in one band:
.TP
.B Overdue
The due date has passed.
.TP
.B Due soon
Due today or within
.B \-\-horizon
days.
.TP
.B Later
Due further out. Counted, not listed.
.PP
Within a band, rows are sorted by days remaining (most overdue first), then
by host count. Each listed row shows the CVE, due date, days remaining
.RB ( today
for zero), host count, Sev rating (with a ransomware marker when CISA lists
known ransomware use) and QIDs.
.PP
KEV entries with a deadline that are not present are counted, not dropped:
those with status
.B UNKNOWN
as
.I coverage UNVERIFIED
(the scanner was not asked, which is not a clean result), everything else as
.IR "not detected here" .
Findings with no usable due date are ignored.
Days are counted in calendar days in UTC.
.PP
When the enrich run recorded a degraded source whose name contains
.BR kev ,
a warning goes to standard error: the catalogue download failed, and a short
overdue list may only mean the deadlines are missing.
.PP
.B cti-kev
reads one file and writes only to standard output and standard error.
It does not contact the scanner, CISA or any mailbox, and does not read
.IR fleet.env .
.SH OPTIONS
Go's flag syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash
.RB ( \-json ),
and a value may follow
.B =
or a space.
.TP
.BI \-\-enriched " FILE"
The enriched JSON file to read.
Default: the newest
.I enriched\-*.json
in
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state ,
chosen by file name (the names carry an ISO date), not by modification time.
The weekly run's
.I weekly\-enriched\-*.json
is never picked.
.TP
.BI \-\-horizon " DAYS"
The
.I due soon
window in days. Not validated; a negative value leaves nothing due soon.
Default:\~\fB14\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-hosts
Add a column of sample host names to the overdue and due-soon tables.
The output then names vulnerable machines; treat it accordingly.
Has no effect with
.BR \-\-json .
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one indented JSON object instead of markdown:
.BR source ,
.BR enriched_generated ,
.BR now ,
.BR horizon_days ,
counts
.BR overdue ,
.BR due_soon ,
.BR later ,
.BR worst_overdue_days ,
.BR ransomware_present ,
.BR not_detected_here ,
.BR coverage_unverified ,
and the CVE lists
.B overdue_cves
and
.BR due_soon_cves .
No host names.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print nothing when nothing is overdue and nothing is due within the horizon,
so a clean day is silent. Applies to the markdown report only:
.B \-\-json
always prints. The degraded-KEV warning on standard error is never
suppressed.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-if\-overdue
Exit 2 when at least one present finding is overdue. Due-soon findings do not
trigger it. For CI and scripts; do not use it in a systemd unit, where it
would mark a working report as a failed unit.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FLEET_HOME
Fleet state root; the default file is looked for in
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state .
Required unless
.B \-\-enriched
is given. Set by the
.B cti\-agent
wrapper and by the systemd units, not read from
.IR fleet.env .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/enriched\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.json
The daily enrich output, written by
.BR run\-digest .
It carries host names; 0600 under the units'
.BR UMask=0077 .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was printed, or suppressed by
.BR \-\-quiet .
Overdue findings do not change this unless
.B \-\-fail\-if\-overdue
is given: being late on a patch is not a failure of this program.
.TP
.B 1
No report: neither
.B \-\-enriched
nor
.B FLEET_HOME
was given, the state directory cannot be read or holds no
.IR enriched\-*.json ,
or the file cannot be read or is not valid JSON.
.TP
.B 2
.B \-\-fail\-if\-overdue
was given and something is overdue. Also returned by Go's flag package for an
unknown option or a bad value, so a script relying on 2 should pass only
options it knows are valid.
.SH EXAMPLES
Today's deadlines, as markdown:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-kev
.EE
.PP
A month's window, with sample hosts:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-kev \-\-horizon 30 \-\-hosts
.EE
.PP
A specific day's file, as JSON:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-kev \e
  \-\-enriched /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/enriched\-2026\-10\-01.json \-\-json
.EE
.PP
In CI, fail the job on anything overdue:
.PP
.EX
cti\-kev \-\-enriched enriched.json \-\-quiet \-\-fail\-if\-overdue
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-digest (1),
.BR cti\-jira (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
README.md, "KEV deadline tracking"; fleet\-kit/README.md, the
.B cti\-kev
section.
